Status: DONE (local implementation); visual acceptance and publication pending
Milestone: Real 3D tabletop handheld with pickup, inspection and native CRT Geom
Dependencies: 05_HARDWARE_UI
Purpose: Replace the flat hardware illustration with an actual, playable 3D
  model while preserving the original emulator and progress-storage contracts.

Tasks:
- [x] Confirm pickup/play/inspection/return interactions and one indigo handheld.
- [x] Confirm warm wood and original cartridge props only; no default games yet.
- [x] Verify the pinned runtime's exact native CRT Geom identifier and behavior.
- [x] Prove live native framebuffer copies work; fix the initially black buffer.
- [x] Pin/package Three.js and its MIT notice through the explicit public allowlist.
- [x] Model front/back/edges, bevels, controls, ports, speaker and battery cover.
- [x] Integrate the live post-shader screen texture and projected physical inputs.
- [x] Add mouse/touch/keyboard inspection, pinch/zoom, reduced motion and failures.
- [x] Preserve saves, remapping, sound, backup recovery and full-scene fullscreen.
- [x] Verify original-demo gameplay and update public docs, images and continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
- Actual 3D mesh geometry and native live frames, not a photograph/CSS3D proxy.
- Click the handheld to lift it; rotate to see its back; return it to the table.
- The default shader is real CRT Geom from the pinned runtime, not a substitute.
- No application or native emulator controls cover the LCD.
- Geometry and physical targets fit desktop, landscape and narrow viewports.
- Inspection/table keyboard gestures do not accidentally control the game.
- Existing ROM/save/backup identities and failure reporting remain intact.
- Local evidence is not human approval or deployment.

Completion evidence:
- 2026-11-04: syntax check PASS; unit suite 9/9 PASS; clean build PASS.
- Final Edge browser suite 13/13 PASS under /BowserBoyAdvance/.
- Native CRT Geom preset verified as shader0 = crt-geom.glsl; real pixel changes
  distinguish filtered/unfiltered frames. Its retained framebuffer is the
  actual CanvasTexture source; held A changes its pixels during live upload.
- Mesh picking, pickup, front/back orientation, return and actual model bounds
  checked at 1366x768, 844x390, 390x844 and 320x568.
- Real touch events verify rotation/pinch, no accidental core input while
  inspecting/on the table, and restored keyboard input in play view.
- All ten shell inputs, mixed-source release, sound/remapping/reload, saved
  progress/backups, automatic timer, failure states and fullscreen still pass.
- Public build is seventeen allowlisted files, including two Three.js modules
  and their license. No ROM collection, private context or full dependency tree.
- Actual table, play, back and original-demo mobile screenshots reviewed.
- No commercial-ROM retest, physical-phone qualification or audible test claimed.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-04: User requested real 3D on a table and default CRT Geom. Confirmed
  lift/play/inspect/return, one indigo console and original cartridge props;
  future default games remain explicitly out of scope.
- 2026-11-04: A live probe proved normal WebGL buffer copies were all black.
  Configured only the emulator canvas before native startup to retain its
  post-shader buffer; repeated samples contained real colored pixels.
- 2026-11-04: Built original Three.js meshes and textures, retained the hidden
  tools drawer and moved keyboard focus to the visible scene canvas.
- 2026-11-04: Screenshot review corrected recessed decals hidden by bevel
  geometry, while runtime tests confirmed the core may use WebGL 1 even though
  the parent 3D renderer requires WebGL 2.
- 2026-11-04: Final 9 unit / 13 real Edge browser cases pass. New design remains
  local and uncommitted; the previously published prototype is not this revision.
- 2026-11-04: User rejected the initial 3D shape and supplied a Sketchfab model.
  Technical test success did not establish visual acceptance. Subsequent
  independently authored reference correction is tracked in workstream 07.
